<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Konstantinos Logothetopoulos</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1878">1878</a>–<a href="/years/1961">1961</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Konstantinos Logothetopoulos was a Greek physician and professor of gynaecology who served as the second collaborationist prime minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/axis-powers">Axis</a> occupation, from December 1942 to April 1943. His government had little authority over the German and Italian occupiers and faced strikes against labour conscription. He was tried after the war and sentenced to life imprisonment, but was released in 1951.</p></div>
